# Grid B — U9 Error handling (per-item vs batch failure)
#
# Gap target: granularity of failure (single-item reject vs whole-
# batch fail) is a specific error-handling dimension with no
# dedicated template. Answer must state a definite behavior, not
# speculate.
#
# Ground truth (internal/tool/emit_evidence.go): per-item reject
# was shipped in session 7 (see memory: "emit_evidence per-item
# reject + line_end auto-swap"). Items with missing anchor_kind are
# rejected individually; the rest of the batch proceeds. A correct
# answer must state this clearly with file:line reference.
ID="u9b"
NAME="error handling — emit_evidence per-item vs batch rejection"
QUESTION="When emit_evidence receives a batch where exactly one item is missing the anchor_kind field, does the whole call fail, or does the rest of the batch succeed and only the bad item get rejected?"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC was 2 question keywords
# — bar = "复述题目". Verified ground truth (`internal/tool/
# emit_evidence.go` line 471-525): per-item reject is shipped (the
# bad item gets rejected, valid items proceed). Tighten by
# requiring the answer to surface (a) the verdict word per-item /
# 单项 / 单条 / partial AND (b) explicit "rest succeed" / "其他
# 通过" / "valid items proceed" semantic — proving the answer
# distinguishes from "whole batch fails".
# 2026-05-14 typed verdict lane: the answer renderer now surfaces the
# canonical `error_granularity_verdict` on principal decision blocks.
# Require the structured verdict token so the eval no longer depends
# only on natural-language synonyms for "per item".
EXPECT_CONTAINS="emit_evidence anchor_kind per_item_rejection"
# 2026-05-08 broaden: model answer correctly stated "仅跳过该 item,
# 其余 item 继续处理" + "部分成功时仍返回 Success: true" — semantic
# match for per-item reject + rest proceed. The original alternation
# (单项/单条/partial; 其余.*接受) missed two natural Chinese phrasings:
#   - "部分" used in "部分成功" — equivalent to "partial" in the
#     case's intent
#   - "其余.*继续(处理|进行)" — equivalent to "rest succeed/proceed",
#     same semantic as "其余.*接受"
# Add both to the alternation; also accept "跳过.*其余" pattern.
# The "speculation/whole-batch-fail" anti-pattern is still blocked by
# EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS below — model cannot ambiguously hedge with
# "unclear / maybe / depends / whole batch".
# 2026-05-08 second-pass broaden: previous regex `其余.*继续(处理|进行)`
# required `继续处理`/`继续进行` ADJACENT, but model wrote
# "其余有效项继续正常处理" (词 between 继续 and 处理) and "其余正常处理"
# (no 继续 verb). Both are clearly the "rest items proceed normally"
# semantic the case wants. Loosen to `(其余|其他).*(处理|进行|接受|通过|成功|继续|正常)`
# so any positive-progress verb after 其余/其他 satisfies it.
# 2026-05-09 third-pass broaden: model wrote "逐项容错机制" (per-item
# fault tolerance) — semantic peer of "per-item" but the regex
# `单项` / `单条` / `部分` didn't include `逐项`, the most natural
# Chinese rendering of "per-item batch processing". Add `逐项` and
# `每项` to the alternation.
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(per.?item|单项|单条|逐项|每项|partial|部分)
(rest.*(succeed|proceed|accept)|valid items|跳过.*其余|(其余|其他).*(处理|进行|接受|通过|成功|继续|正常))"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="unclear maybe depends whole.batch"
